==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cooldown Equality}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*20 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Elephantidae Papaou]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The combination on base hit is a lot to take in, with a Papaou being an immovable brick wall, Ahirujo genuinely being a menace since you can't stack a bunch of Couriers and annihilate him, and Wild Doge being Wild Doge. So how do you beat this one? Cyberstack.

Once you hit the base, spam a bunch of anti-Red units to kill the Capies and Ahirujo as fast as possible. The Red enemies won't be able to move from the combined power of your Cyberpunks and your [[Roe Cat]]s, while Papaou  won't be able to push against the force of [[Cat Egg Pod]].

===Recommended Ubers===
*Backliners with over 420 range: Papaou takes a while to clean up, so bring units to kill him once the stage is over. Examples include [[Joyful Nurse Cat]] and [[God-Emperor Daliasan]].

